+    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
+**metilene** calls differentially methylated regions (DMRs) from bisulfite
+sequencing data. It compares two groups of methylation profiles with a
+two-dimensional statistical test that takes both the methylation level and the
+coverage of each CpG into account.
 
-Detailed documentation of the stand-alone tool metilene is available at
-.. __: http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/Software/metilene/manual.pdf
+-----
 
-The software metilene is available for download at
-.. __: http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/Software/metilene/
-    ]]></help>
+## Outputs
 
+- **DMRs**: all detected DMRs with their adjusted p-value, mean methylation
+  difference, number of CpGs and the mean methylation of both groups.
+- **DMRs (first 4 columns)**: the same regions as chromosome, start, end and
+  adjusted p-value.
+- **Significant DMRs**: the subset of the DMRs above that passes the
+  significance and effect size filters of metilene, as a table and as a
+  bedgraph.
+- **Plots**: PDF with the methylation and the DMR length distributions.
+    ]]></help>
